# Headers tab fixes

In the RequestBuilder headers tab, make these changes:

## 1. Add column header labels
Add a row above the header rows with small muted uppercase labels:
empty column for checkbox, then "Header name", "Value", empty column for delete button.

## 2. Auto Content-Type row
Add a dimmed read-only row at the bottom of user-defined rows showing:
- Header name: Content-Type
- Value: application/json
- Small "auto" badge next to the value
- Checkbox unchecked and disabled
- No delete button
- Inputs are read-only and non-editable
Place this row above the ghost empty row.

## 3. Filtering autocomplete
The header name dropdown should filter as the user types.
If the user typed "x-" only show options starting with "x-".
Dismiss on Escape, select on Enter or click.
Show a "no matches" message if nothing fits.

## 4. Value autocomplete by header name
When a known header name is selected, the value field should suggest common values:
- Content-Type: application/json, application/x-www-form-urlencoded, multipart/form-data
- Accept: application/json, */*
- Authorization: Bearer, Basic

## 5. Dropdown positioning
The dropdown must appear directly below the input it belongs to.
Give it a max-height with scroll if the list is long.